   *
   * After normalization, each column j has zero mean and (up to the epsilon
   * clamp) unit variance, so the Pearson correlation between variables p and q
   * is just the dot product of the corresponding normalized columns:
   *
   *    corr[p][q] = sum_k data[k][p] * data[k][q]
   *
   * In our storage, data[p][k] holds the k-th normalized sample of variable p.
